    "result_text": "The full suite is green (BUILD SUCCESS). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI added a disposable-email-domain blocklist to the `POST /api/owners` pipeline, following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions.\n\n**New files:**\n- `function/owner/DisposableEmailDomains.java` \u2014 the single definition of the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) with a pure `isBlocked(email)` lookup, mirroring the existing `Postcode` helper.\n- `function/owner/EnsureEmailNotDisposable.java` \u2014 an `Ensure`-style step that reads the published `OwnerFieldsDto`, skips when email is absent/blank (email is optional), and throws when the domain is blocked.\n- `escalation/DisposableEmailDomainException.java` \u2014 a checked exception (so it appears in `throws`).\n- `escalation/DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds 400 with `FieldErrorsResponse([\"email\"])`, matching the existing `InvalidEmailExceptionHandler`.\n- `officefloor/escalation/...DisposableEmailDomainException.yml` \u2014 wires the handler.\n\n**Wiring:** inserted the `ensureEmailNotDisposable` step into `owners.POST.yml` right after `normalizeEmail` (so the address is already validated and lower-cased) and before `normalizeAddress`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nEach piece has a single responsibility (blocklist data, the guard step, the error type, the response), and the new step reuses the existing normalization output and error-response conventions rather than duplicating logic. The new acceptance test and the full suite pass.",
